<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!-- Part 14 e2e scenario: the VariableType-sibling counterpart to
     test_vt_objecttype_contradiction.NodeSet2 (ObjectType axis): this one
     overrides a Variable component's own nominal VariableType (not its
     DataType, see test_vt_datatype_contradiction, and not its ValueRank,
     see test_vt_contradiction) to an unrelated sibling VariableType.

     Declares two new VariableTypes, SensorAType and SensorBType, as direct
     siblings under opcua:BaseVariableType (neither a subtype of the
     other), so _add_sibling_type_disjointness(BaseVariableType) asserts
     them pairwise disjoint. BaseType declares Mandatory "Reading" :
     SensorAType. SubType <: BaseType overrides "Reading" to SensorBType, a
     sibling, not a subtype.

     Unlike the ObjectType-axis scenario, a Variable declaration's own type
     change always mints a Virtual Type regardless of local extension (see
     _resolve_target's VariableNodeClass branch: type_changed alone sets
     needs_vt), so this scenario exercises the direct §8/§9 rdfs:subClassOf
     mechanism (VT(SubType, "Reading") ends up subClassOf both SensorBType
     and VT(BaseType, "Reading"), itself subClassOf SensorAType), the same
     mechanism test_vt_contradiction/test_vt_datatype_contradiction rely on,
     not the Functional-property-only mechanism
     test_vt_objecttype_contradiction needs (see that file's own comment).
     Confirmed with the real HermiT reasoner (check_consistency.py's
     expect-contradiction mode). -->
